introduce yourself for the record and then we'll give you three minutes to uh to testify Uh Rob we run our meetings by Robert's rules of order and so in order to keep the decorum in the room all your comments should be directed to me as the chairman of of the committee We shouldn't be going after individual council people And the same thing for our council those comments should be addressed to me also Okay And u we'll look forward to having a a civil discussion and love to hear what you guys have to say on the annexations before us And with that we'll start with Mr Bloom uh who is our city planner Mayor members of the governing body Charles Bloom plan development director Um

just want to just give a little bit of highlights about what's going on with this annexation This is the 10th of our county pocket annexations This is the uh 10th time we've annexed a grouping of properties um based on the city council from 2022's council goal which was facilitated by the mayor and the chief of staff at that time to to come up with those goals And then it's been our task over the course of the last few years to make code modifications and go ahead and us to make the annexations easier and to go ahead and commence with the annexations Um this this property has been one that we um probably had our first interactions with through public comment when uh

Mr David Nicely uh did reach out to our department and we started talking about concerns and questions because they had just recently had a home occupation permit that was approved by the county um about 4 months prior to that council goal being done That was August of 2021 uh that home occupation was approved in such a manner to allow for farming operations and also a farm stand provided not have more than 25 customers daily It was noted in that approval that if it exceeded 25 customers daily it would then need to go through the county site plan process uh with it being a county development adjacent to city streets we frequently deal with these uh

situations where we work with a county and ensure that they have the most painless uh site plan process they can when you're dealing with multiple jurisdictions because in those scenarios you you must deal with our city engineering department No stabs at Tom it's wonderful department Um but you still do need to look at access with with county site plans Today we had a meeting with the nicelys um and their legal representation and we did discuss about how that has worked in the past before We I called it the tale of two McDonald's We have the McDonald's that is located on South Breley Highway at Jefferson where they're making a significant investment in that property and

Jefferson is a street that's in the city For those of you who have driven on Jefferson it's probably to get to the farm stand Um you notice back seven years ago it was uh not a very well-improved road was missing Curb gutter sidewalk on that north side There's some drainage issues because of a natural spring there Well the development for McDonald's was uh doing a lot had a lot of investment So at that time it was reasonable for us to require that in the right ofway they install curb gutter sidewalk and they control the drainage that's coming off of their property The tail of the other McDonald's is just a family name of McDonald Uh

they're located up on Ridge and Greg Way This is one that is presently in development right now and recently has a county site plan that was approved prior to the annexation which we are continuing to honor because that's what we've done and they're on Greg Way which is an unimproved gravel road All they're building is a storage building and a shop Uh it's an expansion of an existing use nearby not very intense low traffic counts not very much traffic that's warranted We again coordinated with the county with through their site plan process and our city engineering department reviewed that application and said you know there's no real rational nexus or a proportionality for us to require full street standards So

essentially what happened with that McDonald property is they signed a uh no protest agreement in the event that the city um moves forward with a local improvement district for upgrade to those roads local improvement districts under the Wyoming state statute They are not handed down or demanded by the governing body or the mayor or any person in staff They are the direct result of a landowner petition um that is sliced and diced in numerous different ways that essentially say 50% of the owners of the land the population of the land It can be by frontage it can be by lot area If they petition the governing body to move forward with that local improvement district then they can do that provide they have a majority that is the will of the land owners It can't be something that is that is um

basically thrown upon them by the governing body without a majority of land owners consent Um and that's just very important why I wanted to mention that when we ask someone to to sign a u a no protest agreement for an improvement district that they understand that it's not just the city it's also the the neighbors that would would create the need for that to actually come to fruition in the future Um with this um proposed annexation we've had two properties that are zoned a that have that have popped up Um we've had the opportunity to meet with both of them the one that's been the most uh vocal and the most public and the one that's garnered the most green ever in the council chambers at the same time Congratulations Um

that's the Wildresh one And we've been trying to make sure that we are making this process as easy for them and predictable for them in the future Um knowing that what they they have in the county right now probably isn't exactly what the county approved And in talking with the county there are concerns um that they have identified that they said "Yes we weren't aware that these items were happening here." But what we want to do is we want to be able to move in work with them on um continuing the operation of this farm as it is allow for livestock and chickens and and animals to continue to be brought into the site you know provided they aren't constituting a nuisance or creating excessive smells flies and

stuff like like that on the site Um we have received the land use documentation form as of Friday And then this afternoon around 11 11:00 a.m we received a very complete and very nice uh site plan drawing packet that was prepared by um Chelsea which is very nice Um which we're we're working on um making sure that we outline any any issues Overall it looks good Um I believe so far all all that staff has seen that are that are issues is wanting to make sure that we um define what an agricultural pile is Is it manure Is it feed Is it farm parts like building parts structure parts Is what what is it So

is it a mixture of all those things together So we can be sure of what those are Um also there's a couple of corrections that they had um noted that just need to be made based on the permanence and the temporary umness of the building There are a couple of outstanding issues that still do exist Um these are issues that would have existed in the city or the county Um a lot of those are with the occupancy of the farm stand structure itself and how it moved into a position where it has electrical connections without inspections without permits Um so those are items that we have um detailed or discussed a a plan with them on what that would look like Um

it doesn't require any removal of sheetrock or inspection of anything in the building It's one just to identify any major life safety or or health issues that are there Um with that we're continue to move forward We hope that this uh annexation can be deemed complete today can be approved today so we can complete the county pocket annexation process Um but we're open for any questions from the governing body and I'm look forward to being able to hopefully close this chapter Thank you Thank you Mr Mayor Three Uh thank you Mr Bloom Um I remember I was rewatching the public services committee You said you defined a little bit of what an urban farm is but it's only policy and

it's not set precedent law Is that correct Mr Blue Mayor Council Men Moody that is correct Um in our unified development code the way our definitions are drafted is they are broad catchall definitions Some development codes are very specific They will go all the way down to a specific use That's a t-shirt shop This is a figurine shop This is a gift shop you know it will say all the different types Ours will say this is a retail service So when someone comes forward and says "We have a t-shirt shop." We're like "Well it's going to fit into this category." And if there's something that is very unclear we will uh basically create these policy documents that are guides which will be published on the website that say this is how we interpret and

this is how it falls into place Um other items we don't specifically call out include uh churches Those are places of of assembly Um like a a massage uh studio or something along those lines Those are personal care So there's all these other ones that just fall into those because we defer to what is the most similar use The urban farm was a little bit different a little bit different operations different scale But through that policy document we put together we said this is what we've captured as an urban farm from what's been provided by the land owner These are the activities that are going and we feel all of those activities fall within these two permitted uses limited agriculture and

general agriculture Um and then we added in and it also includes very limited sales that are ancillary to the overall farming process um that was envisioned to give them comfort that if they wanted to continue to move forward with site expansion in the future that they would be able to do that without any necessary public hearings or running into a roadblock on moving forward They still will have to go through a site plan process which does look at how any uh expansion or change like a new building or a massive change in their operation they'd have to go through to make sure it doesn't have any adverse negative impacts on neighbors Those are impacts such as traffic um

